{"chunk_id": "0d75ccf82883", "text": "Krishna reveals his cosmic nature and explains why Bhishma has been granted the rare vision of his divine form: Bhishma\u2019s unwavering devotion, discipline, and righteousness. Krishna tells the dying warrior that only fifty\u2011six days of life remain before he reaches the realms from which souls do not return, and that the assembled sages seek his final teachings for Yudhishthira, whose judgment is clouded by grief after the war. Bhishma, lying on his bed of arrows, humbly refuses at first, overwhelmed by pain and by the audacity of speaking on duty in Krishna\u2019s presence. In response, Krishna grants him a boon: freedom from pain, perfect clarity of memory, and divine insight so he may instruct the king. The moment becomes sacred, marked by celestial signs, as sages and gods honor Krishna and prepare to hear Bhishma\u2019s teachings.\nKrishna reveals Bhishma\u2019s nearing death, grants him relief and divine clarity, and urges him to teach Yudhishthira while sages witness auspicious signs.\nThemes: divine revelation, approaching death, dharma instruction, grace and devotion, cosmic auspiciousness", "vector": [0.012585132382810116, -0.019367897883057594, 0.0119715491309762, -0.0017757241148501635, -0.007529737427830696, 0.015766430646181107, -0.033240221440792084, -0.011738120578229427, -0.028838427737355232, -0.011858168989419937, 0.01553967036306858, 0.016500061377882957, -0.0033997197169810534, -0.0027311136946082115, -0.006956170313060284, -0.006599357817322016, 0.04764609783887863, 0.004188374616205692, 0.02598392963409424, -0.023316174745559692, 0.012445075437426567, -0.00272444449365139, -0.0025777178816497326, 0.019554641097784042, -0.01895439624786377, 0.01563304290175438, 0.011164553463459015, -0.018941057845950127, -0.005112084560096264, -0.03473416343331337, -0.005598950199782848, 0.005282154306769371, -0.011331288143992424, -0.003914929926395416, -0.024890150874853134, 0.01395235676318407, 0.0092304311692714